Z||000000||David DeVoe||11-14-2001||08:30 AM||||Just did a search in the archives for bra info. The LeBra seems to be the favorite, followed by the Calgon. The wolf bra gets hammered by the critics. How do I get info on the LeBra and Calgon? do they have websites? What auto stores carry them? Anybody know?<BR>Dave||||reg||5
Z||000001||JohnF||11-14-2001||09:02 AM||||LeBra is available anywhere and everywhere from J.C. Whitney to Autozone to O'Reilly's to ??????.<P>Never heard of Calgon Bras.<P>A word of caution, be sure you want one before you buy it.  Be aware they cover nose imperfections well but they also cover (shade) the covered nose area and the result is eventually a two-tone paint job from uneven sun bleaching.<P>Also, LeBra does not make a hood cover for the Fiero, just a bra for the nose.||||reg||6
Z||000002||cadero2dmax||11-14-2001||10:38 AM||||I got mine on e-Bay for $19 (new), there are always Bras being auctioned by a couple from Colorado Springs. They have them all - Wolf, LeBra, etc. <P>G||||reg||1
