Z||000005||tgowens||11-15-2001||01:24 AM||||JohnF, it's Colgan, not Calgon (those are the water softener people......)<P>I have seen LeBra, Wolfe, Colgan all come into the shop........ mostly it's personal preference...... here is mine and why....<P>The Wolfe did not fit right around the wheel wells although I did like the clear plastic over the park lights....... (I had a Wolfe and gave it away)<P>The Colgan covers the hood making it all but impossible to open the hood with the bra in place and, you have to get out of the car to roll up the headlight flaps if you intend on turning on your headlights....... (I have never had a Colgan bra for this reason.<P>The LeBra is my personal choice and I have one for all five of my '87GT's. The hood opens smoothly (although it <I>is</I> left uncovered. and it is easy to remove. The LeBra was the preferred option from Pontiac when the Fiero was being sold and evidently many of them had them (I can attest to that by all of the bra clips that I have removed from parts cars!)<P>Victoria's Secret? Another personal favorite of mine although I really don't see many of them come into the shop (guess I'm in the wrong kind of shop!)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
